## 6. Toggles and callouts
### 6.1 Standard toggle

```text
<details color="gray_bg">
<summary>Implementation details</summary>
	Child paragraph
	- Child list item
</details>
```

The child content must be indented.

Keep `<summary>` directly inside `<details>` and use it only for the toggle title.
### 6.2 Toggle heading

```text
## Detailed acceptance criteria {toggle="true" color="blue"}
	- Criterion one
	- Criterion two
```

### 6.3 Callout

```text
<callout icon="💡" color="yellow_bg">
	**Key assumption**
	The design assumes one active lease per worker.
</callout>
```

Every block inside a callout must be indented.
### 6.4 BMAD usage
Recommended use:

- assumptions → yellow callout
- architecture decisions → purple callout
- blockers → red callout
- validation outcome → green callout
- background context → blue callout

Do not use a callout only for visual decoration.

