## 9. Code blocks and Mermaid diagrams
### 9.1 Code block

````text
```javascript
const value = "Do not escape [brackets] or *asterisks* here";
```
````

Code-block content is literal. Do not escape Markdown characters inside it.

Always specify a language when known.
### 9.2 Mermaid

````text
```mermaid
flowchart TD
	A["Client (Web UI)"] -->|MCP request| B["Notion API"]
```
````

For stable Mermaid rendering:

- quote labels containing parentheses, colons, brackets, or punctuation
- use `<br>` for line breaks inside node labels
- keep node IDs simple and alphanumeric
- avoid raw Markdown formatting inside Mermaid labels
- validate complex diagrams before publishing

For large BMAD architecture diagrams, prefer multiple focused diagrams over one oversized diagram.

