## 10. Media and files
Supported enhanced-markdown media blocks include:

```text
![Caption](URL) {color="gray"}

<audio src="URL" color="gray">Caption</audio>
<video src="URL" color="gray">Caption</video>
<pdf src="URL" color="gray">Caption</pdf>
<file src="URL" color="gray">Caption</file>
```

Rules:

- Use a stable HTTPS URL or the file URI returned by the relevant upload tool.
- Treat pre-signed URLs returned from Notion as temporary.
- Do not invent upload identifiers.
- Do not use `<embed>` as a guaranteed enhanced-markdown block. Third-party embeds, bookmarks, and link previews may be returned as unsupported `<unknown>` blocks and may require a dedicated Notion tool or block API.

