## 17. BMAD document styling rules
### 17.1 Recommended page structure
```text
# Document title

<callout icon="📌" color="blue_bg">
	**Document type:** Architecture / PRD / Epic / Story / ADR
	**Status:** Draft
	**Owner:** Name or team
	**Last updated:** Date
</callout>

<table_of_contents color="gray"/>
## Executive summary
## Context
## Goals
## Non-goals
## Requirements
## Architecture or approach
## Risks and mitigations
## Decisions
## Open questions
## Acceptance criteria
## Next actions
```

Adjust the sections to the BMAD artifact type.
### 17.2 Heading discipline
- one `#` heading for the page title
- `##` for major sections
- `###` for subsections
- `####` only for local detail
- do not skip levels without a clear reason
- do not use headings as decorative labels
### 17.3 Lists versus paragraphs
Use lists for:

- requirements
- acceptance criteria
- decisions
- risks
- tasks
- constraints
- concise alternatives

Use paragraphs for reasoning, narrative, trade-offs, and explanatory context.
### 17.4 Acceptance criteria
Prefer checklists:

```text
## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] API returns `202 Accepted` for asynchronous requests.
- [ ] The response includes `job_id`, `status_url`, and `status`.
- [ ] Unknown or evicted jobs return `404`.
```

### 17.5 Decision records

```text
<callout icon="🏛️" color="purple_bg">
	**Decision:** Use an in-process LRU job store for the first release.
	**Rationale:** The initial deployment is single-instance and does not require cross-node durability.
</callout>
```

### 17.6 Risks

```text
<table fit-page-width="true" header-row="true">
	<tr>
		<td>**Risk**</td>
		<td>**Impact**</td>
		<td>**Mitigation**</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td>Process restart clears jobs</td>
		<td>Medium</td>
		<td>Document as a v1 limitation and migrate to durable storage before horizontal scaling.</td>
	</tr>
</table>
```

